# Dockerfile's final stage does `COPY . .` with no exclusions — every file
# in this directory landed in the image, unpacked onto the container's own
# disk. On skolab-backend-py's small Render free-tier ephemeral disk, that
# tripped the app's own >80% disk-usage alert (app/main.py's
# monitor_disk_space). This file is the actual fix: keep dev/test/CI-only
# artifacts out of the build context entirely, not just out of git.
#
# Two of these (dev.db, _t.db) were also committed to git by accident —
# tests/conftest.py's SQLite fallback generates them locally, and nothing
# in .gitignore caught the pattern before now (see the accompanying
# .gitignore change). This file stops them re-entering a future image even
# though old commits still carry their old contents; a .dockerignore entry
# alone can't undo what git already tracked, only what gets built next.

# Local dev / test artifacts
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
.env
.env.*
.coverage
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Dev/CI-only tooling and scripts — not imported by the runtime app
tests/
scripts/
ci_bootstrap_db.py
docker-compose.yml
pytest.ini
ruff.toml
requirements-dev.txt

# VCS metadata — irrelevant at runtime, meaningful size in a monorepo clone
.git/
.gitignore

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
